# GitHub organization enforces 2FA on all members
# Platform: GitHub (SDLC::Organization assets)
# CTN: github_org_settings
# Frameworks: KSI-IAM-SNU, CMMC IA.L2-3.5.3, NIST IA-2(1), IA-2(2)

META
    esp_id `github-org-2fa-enforced-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `github`
    criticality `high`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `SDLC::Organization`

    title `GitHub organization enforces 2FA on members`
    description `Validates that the GitHub organization has the "Require two-factor authentication for everyone in this organization" setting enabled. Without org-level enforcement, individual member accounts may rely on password-only authentication, exposing the entire orgs repository fleet to credential-theft compromise.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `github,org,identity,mfa,ksi-iam-snu,cmmc-ia-l2-3.5.3,nist-ia-2-1`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-SNU,CMMC:IA.L2-3.5.3,NIST-800-53:IA-2(1),NIST-800-53:IA-2(2)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-SNU,IA.L2-3.5.3`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `GitHub:scanset:identity-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `In the GitHub organization settings, navigate to "Authentication security" and enable "Require two-factor authentication for everyone in the org". Note that members without 2FA will be removed from the org when this is turned on, so coordinate with affected users beforehand.`

    component_id `comp-github-identity`

    impl_KSI_IAM_SNU `Standard named users on the SDLC integration platform are required to authenticate with a second factor. The GitHub organization "two_factor_requirement_enabled" setting is the enforcement primitive: when enabled, members without 2FA are removed from the org at the identity providers layer rather than relying on per-member self-attestation. The CTN reads this flag at scan time and emits a finding when it is false.`
    impl_IA_L2_3_5_3 `Multi-factor authentication is enforced for non-privileged accounts at the GitHub organization boundary. The "two_factor_requirement_enabled" flag on the GET /orgs/{login} endpoint reports whether GitHub removes members lacking 2FA from the organization at the identity providers layer. Enforcement at the identity layer is preferred over per-member auditing because it cannot be bypassed by an individual member configuration change.`

META_END

DEF
    # Default placeholder value, overridden per-asset by PolicySetSync
    # at bind time. PolicySetSync rewrites the SET body with one OBJECT
    # per bound org, each carrying that org's concrete login.
    VAR login string `_unbound_`

    # Bound assets - managed programmatically by PolicySetSync from
    # inventory.asset_policies (status = active). Do not hand-edit;
    # the SET body is the only mutable region of this file.
    SET github_orgs union
        OBJECT org_target
            login VAR login
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE org_enforces_2fa
        found boolean = true
        two_factor_requirement_enabled boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN github_org_settings
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF org_enforces_2fa
            SET_REF github_orgs
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
